# StyleMeUp · Cursor rules

You are working in the StyleMeUp repo. Before generating any code or copy, read:

1. `DESIGN.md` — the brand bible. **The document wins over your generation, every time.**
2. `AGENTS.md` — engineering conventions for AI agents.

## Two laws

1. **`DESIGN.md` is the contract.** Every line of code, color, motion timing, and copy must trace back to a section. If you can't cite one, ask before generating.
2. **The blank screen is the enemy.** No empty states. No skeleton loaders >400ms. Every wait is editorial.

## The two registers

- **Magazine** = `--void #000000` true black. Discover, trend features, look reveals. Monumental UPPERCASE display, full-bleed cinematic imagery. Voice: declarative, verbless, final.
- **Sanctuary** = `--paper #FFFFFF` true white. Closet, capture, settings. Lowercase italic display, generous whitespace. Voice: hushed, intimate, lowercase.

**Never mix registers on one screen.** Every screen file declares its register at the top:

```ts
/**
 * @register Magazine
 * @design-ref DESIGN.md §1.5, §10
 */
```

## Tokens are sacred

Import every color, type, spacing, and timing value from `tokens/`. Never hard-code. If a value isn't in `tokens/`, add it there first with a comment citing `DESIGN.md`.

```ts
// ❌ never
backgroundColor: '#000000'

// ✓ always
import { colors } from '@/tokens';
backgroundColor: colors.void
```

## Hard bans (from DESIGN.md §4)

Visual: purple/blue gradients · glassmorphism · rounded corners ≥8px on cards/buttons · Material drop shadows · stock photography · AI-generated faces · gradients on text · pattern backgrounds.

Copy: sparkle emoji ✨ · "Powered by AI" · "Let's…" · exclamation points outside error recovery · "magic/smart/intelligent/amazing" · onboarding cheerfulness · ANY emoji in product UI.

Layout: dashboard layouts · masonry · side rails on mobile · tab bars >4 items · modals for benign actions · two registers on one screen.

Motion: spring physics on chrome · parallax on text · 3D card flips · autoplay sound · pulse animations on CTAs · bounce-in modals.

## The Vogue test

Before any string ships, ask: *would this sentence appear, verbatim, in a Vogue or Burberry campaign?* If no, rewrite. If still no, delete.

## Stack — don't deviate

Expo + React Native + TypeScript + Reanimated 3 + Skia. Backend Supabase. Web prototype Next.js 15 + Tailwind. Don't propose alternatives without surfacing the reason.

## Performance budget

LCP <2.0s mid-range mobile · The Vanishing 60fps on iPhone 13/Pixel 6 baseline · first-screen JS <200KB.

## When unsure

Surface it. Don't fabricate. Saying *"DESIGN.md doesn't specify X — asking before generating"* is preferred over guessing.

Pushing back on a brief that would violate DESIGN.md is part of the job. Cite the section, propose an alternative, ask for an exception if needed.
